cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Negative controls in citizen-science estimates of wildfire
  effects on birds
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite both the software and the
  paper it accompanies.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ethan
    family-names: Le
repository-code: "TODO-GITHUB-URL"
abstract: >-
  Replication package for a study joining eBird checklists, MTBS
  burn severity and MODIS vegetation indices across California,
  2015-2026. Nineteen bird species across four habitat groups,
  including three negative-control species that wildfire cannot
  plausibly affect. The extent-based design fails its own
  falsification test: all three controls register larger fire
  effects than the focal species, and after a square burns
  birders visit 42% fewer distinct locations inside it.
keywords:
  - citizen science
  - eBird
  - wildfire severity
  - negative controls
  - observer bias
  - difference-in-differences
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-08-23"
